  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 119 AM MDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nSunday sees the remnants of the aforementioned MCV/disturbance still \nover west-central NM, likely enhancing afternoon thunderstorm \nactivity there again another day. Another round of flash flooding \nimpacts from slow moving and rain efficient storms will need to be \nwatched in this area again Sunday afternoon. Lesser storm coverage \nwill be favored further east along and east of the central mountain \nchain where highs climb back into the low 100s. \n\nThereafter, next week will feature a dominant monsoon high loitering \nover the Four Corners region or just east of there. Daily rounds of \nafternoon thunderstorms developing over the high terrain before \nmoving westward to southwestward over surrounding lower elevations \nwill be the rule each day. Moderate to high heat risk will remain \nover the lower elevations of central and eastern NM where highs \nclimb into the upper 90s to low 100s.",
